 ## Overview
-Alpha Grid Mask is a module that samples alpha (opacity) values from a precomputed 3D alpha volume using grid sampling with normalized coordinates [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial]. It enables efficient ray filtering based on opacity by providing a differentiable interface to query alpha values at arbitrary 3D coordinates [S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from sibling interpolation methods by specifically targeting alpha/mask volumes for culling or weighting, often leveraging hardware-accelerated grid sampling routines (e.g., PyTorch's `grid_sample`) rather than manual kernel implementations [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
